## Why This Is Asked

Tests distributed feature flags and canary rollouts, focusing on cross-service consistency, latency budgets, and rollback safety in high-scale environments.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags, canary rollout
- Contract tests across services
- Observability and alerting
- Rollback safety and kill switches
- Traffic shaping and data mocks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example contract test scaffold (pseudo)
test('FlagPropagation', () => {
  const v1 = flag.get('newCheckout');
  expect(v1.UI).toEqual(v1.API);
  // simulate latency
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate rollback in case of divergent flag values?
- What metrics and traces would you rely on to trigger rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests for streaming pipelines are critical at scale; this angle emphasizes end-to-end guarantees, replay safety, and schema evolution beyond static REST tests.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming end-to-end testing with Kafka
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once semantics
- Windowed aggregations correctness
- Schema evolution and compatibility
- Backpressure and fault injection
- Canary deployments and CI validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo test: idempotent ingestion with duplicate events
function testIdempotentIngestion() {
  const events = generateEvents({n: 1000, duplicates: true});
  ingest(events);
  ingest(events);
  const result = readWindowedAggStore();
  assert(result.latestWindowSum === expectedSum);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model time in tests for replay vs processing time?
- How would you verify exactly-once semantics with out-of-order events?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests for event-driven flows are common in production; beginners should grasp end-to-end testing, idempotency, and failure handling.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end testing of queues and email sinks
- Idempotent processing of events
- Retries, backoff, and dead-letter queues
- Isolation of external dependencies in CI

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple idempotent handler skeleton
const seen = new Set();
function handleEvent(event){
  if (seen.has(event.id)) return;
  seen.add(event.id);
  sendEmail(event.userEmail, 'Welcome!', {eventId: event.id});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the dead-letter path for poison messages?
- How would you simulate email service outage and verify retry/backoff behavior?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests must demonstrate isolation and safety when rolling out tenant-specific features behind feature flags at scale, including data privacy, quota enforcement, and rollback reliability.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant data isolation
- Feature flags and canary strategies
- Per-tenant contracts and synthetic data
- Audit trails and rollback safety
- Data backups and retention compliance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test scaffold to validate cross-tenant data isolation
function testTenantIsolation(tenantA, tenantB) {
  const dA = query(tenantA, 'billing');
  const dB = query(tenantB, 'billing');
  assert(dA.tenantId === tenantA.id);
  assert(dB.tenantId === tenantB.id);
  assert(!dA.data.includes(tenantB.id));
  assert(!dB.data.includes(tenantA.id));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect tenant leakage during a schema migration?
- How would you measure the overhead of per-tenant isolation at scale?

## Why This Is Asked

Feature flags and canary rollouts are common in production, but testing them across regions with multi-tenant overrides is tricky. This question probes how you design end-to-end tests, ensure isolation, observe, and roll back safely.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flag resolution with per-user and per-tenant overrides
- Canary rollout across multiple regions
- Observability: traces, metrics, and logs
- Rollback safety and data isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example test skeleton for flag resolution
describe('Flag resolution', () => {
  it('applies user-level overrides and region-specific rules', () => {
    const ctx = {userId:'u1', tenant:'t1', region:'eu-west-1', featureFlags:{newFeature:'on'}};
    expect(resolveFlag(ctx)).toBe(true);
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you simulate a region failure mid-rollout and verify rollback?
- How would you validate no cross-tenant data leakage during experiments?

